      "side": 1,
      "message": "`putfo` writes straight to the final path, so if the transfer dies part-way (dropped connection, ENOSPC on the host, sftp timeout) `/root/\u003ccloud\u003e_instackenv.json` is left truncated and the previous good copy is already gone. Those files feed `overcloud deploy` / openshift tooling directly, so a half-written inventory is worse than a missing one. Uploading to `remote_path + \".tmp\"` and then `sftp.posix_rename(tmp, remote_path)` (falling back to remove+rename) makes the publish atomic.",
      "revId": "2321d9432a06a85f601099bc97e504155f434894",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
